        "message": "Fix indentation when the indent character is not ASCII\n\nIndentation tracks current_indent_len as a byte index into its indents\ncache, but grew and shrank it by indent_size, a count of characters.\nWriter::new_with_indent takes a u8 and char::from turns any byte above\n0x7F into a two byte character, so the index landed inside a character\nand the slice in current() panicked, or one level of indent came out\nhalf as wide as asked for.\n\nSerializer::indent takes a char and passed it on as `indent_char as u8`,\nwhich truncated every non-ASCII character to a byte and emitted control\ncharacters instead.",
        "tree": {
          "sha": "4224ee574d3fa258a0c9a4d71dd499652ec7b9db",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/tafia/quick-xml/git/trees/4224ee574d3fa258a0c9a4d71dd499652ec7b9db"
        },
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/tafia/quick-xml/git/commits/76db56fcdc1e1bcd21ef31b8dd6304df05a2c916",
        "comment_count": 0,
        "verification": {
          "verified": false,
          "reason": "unsigned",
          "signature": null,
          "payload": null,
          "verified_at": null
        }
      }
